<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-27T21:19:15+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:19:15 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[US charges 48 non-citizens in election-related cases across five states; two Indians named]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135239322.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The US Justice Department has announced charges against 48 non-citizens in election-related cases across Pennsylvania, California, Florida, New York and Nevada. Two Indian nationals are among those accused. The cases involve allegations of illegal voting in federal elections, fraudulent voter registration and false claims of US citizenship, including alleged misrepresentations in naturalisation proceedings. All defendants are presumed innocent.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-charges-48-non-citizens-over-election-related-crimes-in-pennsylvania-california-florida-new-york-and-nevada-two-indians-among-those-accused-of-illegal-voting-and-false-citizenship-claims/articleshow/135239322.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-charges-48-non-citizens-over-election-related-crimes-in-pennsylvania-california-florida-new-york-and-nevada-two-indians-among-those-accused-of-illegal-voting-and-false-citizenship-claims/articleshow/135239322.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T21:16:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135239448,imgsize-108500.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Maine woman wins federal court battle over faulty $189,471 foreclosure notice]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135238779.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a landmark decision, a federal court upheld that Maine's foreclosure notification regulations extend protections to non-borrowing spouses. This case highlighted a scenario where a woman faced foreclosure due to her husband's refinancing actions, taken without her consent. The lender's notice was found lacking in clarity regarding amounts owed, underscoring the critical need for adherence to state laws which safeguard homeowners from improper foreclosure practices.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2005-a-maine-husband-refinanced-the-family-home-without-his-wifes-signature-after-their-divorce-and-years-without-payments-a-faulty-189471-foreclosure-notice-helped-her-win-in-federal-court/articleshow/135238779.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2005-a-maine-husband-refinanced-the-family-home-without-his-wifes-signature-after-their-divorce-and-years-without-payments-a-faulty-189471-foreclosure-notice-helped-her-win-in-federal-court/articleshow/135238779.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T21:11:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135238923,imgsize-85888.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California river restoration project attracts salmon within days of completion]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135238601.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable effort in California involved restoration crews who revitalized a section of the Lower Tuolumne River, focusing on creating vital salmon habitats and enriching local biodiversity. The project saw the introduction of over 24,000 cubic yards of gravel and 80 boulders, which collectively improved spawning conditions. Almost immediately after the work was completed, salmon flocked to the newly established habitats, showcasing the project's success.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/california-crews-placed-over-24000-cubic-yards-of-gravel-49-trees-and-80-boulders-in-the-tuolumne-river-to-rebuild-4-78-acres-of-habitat-within-days-of-completion-scientists-documented-salmon-spawning-on-new-riffles/articleshow/135238601.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/california-crews-placed-over-24000-cubic-yards-of-gravel-49-trees-and-80-boulders-in-the-tuolumne-river-to-rebuild-4-78-acres-of-habitat-within-days-of-completion-scientists-documented-salmon-spawning-on-new-riffles/articleshow/135238601.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T21:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135238744,imgsize-192444.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why not remove H-1Bs: Alleged leaked messages show Microsoft workers questioning exit package amid Green Card row]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135238674.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-not-remove-h-1bs-alleged-leaked-messages-show-microsoft-workers-questioning-exit-package-amid-green-card-row/articleshow/135238674.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-not-remove-h-1bs-alleged-leaked-messages-show-microsoft-workers-questioning-exit-package-amid-green-card-row/articleshow/135238674.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T20:54:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135239049,imgsize-44646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Georgia businessman jailed for 15 years for $76m Ponzi scheme targeting 300+ investors]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135237028.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Edwin Brant Frost IV, a businessman from Georgia, has received a 15-year prison sentence following his involvement in a Ponzi scheme that deceived more than 300 investors. This fraudulent operation caused a staggering loss of $76 million. Presenting himself as a reliable lender, Frost was actually battling significant financial turmoil. He misappropriated investors' money for his lavish lifestyle and political donations while neglecting loan repayments.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-georgia-businessman-promised-investors-8-to-18-returns-from-small-business-loans-but-diverted-funds-to-luxury-spending-and-politics-he-has-been-sentenced-to-15-years-over-a-76-million-ponzi-scheme/articleshow/135237028.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-georgia-businessman-promised-investors-8-to-18-returns-from-small-business-loans-but-diverted-funds-to-luxury-spending-and-politics-he-has-been-sentenced-to-15-years-over-a-76-million-ponzi-scheme/articleshow/135237028.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T19:51:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135237462,imgsize-622628.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MIT students tackle lunar waste with recycling system]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135237075.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[MIT students have pioneered a revolutionary recycling solution aimed at mitigating waste buildup on the Moon. As new supplies begin to arrive, it is vital to have efficient methods for dealing with packaging waste. This ambitious project, which has garnered accolades from NASA, seeks to transform waste into useful materials for lunar bases, setting a precedent for potential sustainability improvements both on the Moon and Earth.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-the-mit-students-who-built-a-system-that-turns-lunar-waste-into-useful-materials-for-future-moon-missions-winning-both-tracks-of-nasas-lunarecycle-challenge-and-925000-in-prizes/articleshow/135237075.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-the-mit-students-who-built-a-system-that-turns-lunar-waste-into-useful-materials-for-future-moon-missions-winning-both-tracks-of-nasas-lunarecycle-challenge-and-925000-in-prizes/articleshow/135237075.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T20:07:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135237160,imgsize-